          ":question/id": "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-141215",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A) &={R}^{6} \\\\ \\text{dim(Col}(A)) &=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\ \\text{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) &=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,\u2713$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""
        },
