          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-47604",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)\u2282{R}^{n},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{rank}(A)=n$\n\nII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,\u21d4\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)\u2282{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{rank}(A)=n.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)\u2282{R}^{n},$ then we have $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))\\le n-1\\ne n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)\u2282{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$* $\\,\u2713$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)\u2282{R}^{n},$ then  $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\,\\times$  \n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)\u2282{R}^{n},$ the matrix $A$ can have at most  $n-1$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""
        },
